    <fr:title text="Lifecycle of a JAX program">Lifecycle of a JAX program</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>We have the following compilation pipeline</html:p>
    <html:ol><html:li>Tracing: Python / JAX -&gt; <fr:link href="/G981/" title="jaxpr" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G981/" display-uri="G981" type="local">jaxpr</fr:link></html:li>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:code>jax.make_jaxpr(fun)(*args)</html:code></html:li>
    <html:li>Abstract execution. JAX executes python code using abstract tracer objects instead of real arrays.</html:li>
    <html:li>Every operation and its intermediate result is recorded into <fr:link href="/G981/" title="jaxpr" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G981/" display-uri="G981" type="local">jaxpr</fr:link>.</html:li>
    <html:li>Sequence used to construct a grap, which the XLA compiler will later optimize.</html:li>
    <html:li>Python code is executed once during tracing but excluded from final graph.</html:li>
    <html:li>Each JAX primitive registers functions for</html:li>
    <html:ul><html:li>Lowering to StableHLO</html:li>  
        <html:li>How it is transformed under <html:code>grad</html:code> and <html:code>vmap</html:code>.</html:li></html:ul></html:ul>
  <html:li>Lowering: Jaxpr -&gt; HLO</html:li>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:code>fn_lowered = jax.jit(fun).lower(*args)</html:code></html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>stable_hlo = fn_lowered.as_text()</html:code></html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>hlo = fn_lowered.compiler_ir('hlo')</html:code></html:li>
    <html:li>Multiple ML frameworks lower to StableHLO.</html:li>
    <html:ul><html:li>Hardware agnostic.</html:li>
      <html:li>Backwards compatible.</html:li></html:ul></html:ul>
  <html:li>Compile: HLO -&gt; Optimized HLO -&gt; LLO IR -&gt; VLIW -&gt; Executables</html:li>
  <html:ul><html:li><html:code>compiled = fn_lowered.compile()</html:code></html:li>
    <html:li><html:code>compiled.runtime_executable()</html:code> returns a <html:code>LoadedExecutable</html:code>.</html:li>
    <html:li>Useful(?) <html:code>compiled.cost_analysis()</html:code>.</html:li>
    <html:li>HLO:</html:li>
    <html:ul><html:li>Input for XLA compiler.</html:li>
      <html:li>Directed acyclic graph of copmutational operations.</html:li>
      <html:li>All array dimensions are known at compile time.</html:li>
      <html:li>Limited opcodes i.e. Add, Multiply, Transpose, Dot, etc.</html:li></html:ul></html:ul></html:ol>
  </fr:mainmatter>
